--- body ---

## Context

Four harness warts are documented in the 1024 journal (2026-10-06).
Two are already fixed in code (unloaded assertion local-only;
judged3 + idempotent judge seats) — keep them fixed. Two remain
workarounds:

1. MAX_ATTEMPTS is LIFETIME, not per-pass: re-passes need manual
   runs-void archiving to free poisoned legs. Make the attempt cap
   pass-aware (a pass context or a cap that resets per driver run).
2. stop-arm.sh vram-wait polls BOTH GPUs under 800/600 MiB while arm
   A's resident server legitimately holds VRAM: every stop burns its
   full 180s and a wrap-up takes ~15 min. Make vram-wait scoped to the
   arms actually being torn down (exclude the arm being kept).

## Exit criteria

- [x] Both fixes in, with a smoke pass on 0470 to verify no regression
- [x] A re-pass observed to free legs without manual archiving
- [x] Wrap-up observed under 2 min with arm A resident
